# X-Downloader .gitignore: an ALLOW-LIST. Everything is ignored unless a "!" line below lists it.
#
# Why: a deny-list can only name the files somebody thought of (cookies.txt, settings.json ...). A cookie
# export called x.com_cookies.txt, a .env, a screenshot or a log slipped through, and "git add ." would have
# published a login session. With an allow-list a file nobody listed is never picked up by "git add ." or
# "git add -A": forgetting an entry means a file is NOT committed (you notice at once), never a leak.
#
# To track a new kind of file, add a "!" line for it. tests/test_secret_guard.py fails when a tracked file is
# not covered here, and when a file of an unknown kind would be picked up.
#
# What the program writes into this folder, all ignored by the first rule: cookies.txt and cookies_<domain>.txt
# (session tokens!), settings.json, list.txt, failed_list.txt, *.log, .processing.list, downloader.lock, the
# downloaded videos, yt-dlp and ffmpeg (auto-downloaded), .runtime/ (the unpacked runtime) and .tmp/.
/*

!/.gitignore

!/start_gui.sh
!/LICENSE*
!/requirements.txt
!/*.md

# Folders are allowed, but inside them only these kinds of file.
!/bundled-runtime/
/bundled-runtime/*
!/bundled-runtime/README.md
!/bundled-runtime/linux-*.tar.gz

# The screenshots of the README: PNGs directly in docs/images/, nothing else in docs/. tools/check-secrets.sh lets
# exactly these paths through as binary files; change the two together.
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/images/
/docs/images/*
!/docs/images/*.png



!/tests/
/tests/*
!/tests/*.py

!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/*.sh
!/tools/githooks/
/tools/githooks/*
!/tools/githooks/pre-*

!/xdownloader/
/xdownloader/*
!/xdownloader/*.py

# Publish: the agent rules stay in the private development repo. These two lines keep them out of "git add" when a local copy is recreated.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
